## The 9 blockers and their fixes (all in session_restore.rs)

(1) Production wiring via callable entry points (owned file):
    startup_session_manager() (serve + live flag), login_restore_plan()
    (load + plan vs installed_apps + merge_autostart + queue placements),
    logout_save() (collect + save at default path), launch_plan() runner,
    launch_desktop_id() (resolve .desktop at restore time, spec Exec
    expansion, detached setsid spawn, reaper thread so no zombies),
    PendingPlacements (tag-then-app FIFO matching), apply_restored_placement()
    (move_to_workspace + resize/move-delta + fullscreen/maximize/minimize).
    Call-site hooks in runtime.rs/windows.rs/shell are NOT mine to edit;
    exact patch snippets are in "Excluded-file patch snippets" below.
(2) register() cleanup ids are discarded ids ONLY; a second live instance
    gets a fresh id with empty cleanup. deleted() only forgets discarded ids.
(3) Registry keeps InstanceRecord{id, dbus_name, crashed} per app (GNOME
    SavedApp shape): register reuses a non-running prior id (or next_id
    leftover); note_name_owner_changed() replicates on_instance_vanished
    (clears name, marks crashed, feeds the crash set); serve thread runs a
    NameOwnerChanged MatchRule subscription feeding the hook.
    On-disk instance persistence deliberately NOT added: instance ids are
    tokens and the secrets policy forbids recording tokens.
(4) WindowPlacement::validated uses saturating_abs(); i32::MIN rejects.
(5) load_from checks metadata size AND caps the stream with take(MAX+1);
    /dev/zero-style unbounded inputs terminate as Corrupt.
(6) default_autostart_dirs honors absolute XDG_CONFIG_HOME (relative
    ignored per spec); scan_autostart requires Type=Application + non-empty
    Exec; config-only entries skip WITHOUT retaining the stem (system
    same-stem entry still loads); Hidden/disabled stubs still shadow.
(7) save_to uses a unique O_EXCL temp (.session.<pid>.<nanos>.<ctr>.tmp)
    + file fsync + rename + directory fsync; parallel saves only contend
    on the final rename, never interleave; mode stays 0600.
(8) register_with_sender falls back empty dbus_name to the D-Bus caller
    (gsm-manager.c behavior); unknown UnregisterRestore answers
    org.gnome.SessionManager.Error.NotRegistered ("Provided instance not
    found", GSM_MANAGER_ERROR_NOT_REGISTERED parity).
(9) Fetched gnome-session 51.0 gsm-manager.c, gsm-session-save.c,
    org.gnome.SessionManager.xml and gsm-session-save.h. Verified:
    signatures RegisterRestore(s,s)->(u,s,as), DeletedInstanceIds(s,as),
    UnregisterRestore(s,s), RestoreSupported read-only bool; reason codes
    0 PRISTINE / 1 LAUNCH / 2 RECOVER / 3 RESTORE match our constants and
    the XML's documented meanings. Corrected the top-of-file description:
    gsm-manager.c hardcodes RestoreSupported FALSE ("For GNOME 50, we've
    disabled the save/restore feature") -- GNOME 50/51 never restores.
    Tuna keeps REAL restoration (opt-in), same contract shapes. No descope:
    plan/restore/launcher/placement all stay and are now wired.
    Deliberate divergences documented: truthful RestoreSupported +
    in-registry (not on-disk) instance continuity per the secrets policy.

