## Excluded-file patch snippets (union-time call sites; NOT applied)

These hooks live in files outside this lane. Each snippet is exact against
the f9a57b3c tree; line numbers are from that tree.

### A. runtime.rs -- startup + login (in run(), after Runtime::launch)

Location: crates/compositor/src/runtime.rs, in `run()` right after
`let (mut runtime, mut event_loop) = Runtime::launch(session)?;` (~line 5435).

```rust
// P-SY-08 (#338): serve the restore facade, then restore.
let restore_supported = crate::session_restore::startup_session_manager();
let login = crate::session_restore::login_restore_plan(
    crate::session_restore::RestorePrefs {
        enabled: std::env::var_os("TUNA_RESTORE").is_some_and(|v| v == "1"),
    },
    &runtime.supervisor_crashed_apps(), // union: real per-app crash set
);
for attempt in crate::session_restore::launch_plan(
    &login.entries,
    &|req| crate::session_restore::launch_desktop_id(&req.desktop_id),
) {
    if let Err(e) = attempt.result {
        eprintln!(
            "tuna-compositor: restore: {} failed: {e}",
            attempt.desktop_id
        );
    }
}
runtime.manager_mut().set_pending_restore(login.placements); // needs snippet C
```

Notes: the shell preference UI (excluded shell files) owns the persisted
opt-in bool and must push it into `restore_supported` (store(bool)) and
into the login prefs; TUNA_RESTORE here is only a stopgap default. The
`supervisor_crashed_apps` accessor does not exist yet; wire the real
supervisor crash record at union.

### B. runtime.rs -- logout/shutdown save (both run() exit paths)

Location: crates/compositor/src/runtime.rs, `run()`: (i) inside
`if shutdown.load(...)` before `restore_env(prev_env)` (~line 5489), and
(ii) in the `done =>` arm before `restore_env(prev_env)` (~line 5518).
Both call one helper; add it next to `run()`:

```rust
// P-SY-08 (#338): snapshot mapped toplevels at shutdown. Uses only
// public WindowManager/StateModel accessors; tags resolve where the
// surface is at hand (map path), else None (app-id matching still works).
fn save_session_for_shutdown(runtime: &mut Runtime) {
    use crate::session_restore::{logout_save, RestorePrefs, WindowPlacement, WindowRow};
    use crate::windows::WindowLayout;
    let prefs = RestorePrefs {
        enabled: runtime.restore_enabled(), // union: shell-pushed preference
    };
    if !prefs.enabled {
        return;
    }
    let active = runtime.manager().model().active_workspace();
    let rows = runtime.manager().model().windows().filter_map(|entry| {
        let geo = runtime.manager().geometry(entry.id)?;
        let layout = runtime.manager().window_layout(entry.id)?;
        let floating = matches!(layout, WindowLayout::Floating);
        Some(WindowRow {
            desktop_id: None, // union: fill from the app-id -> desktop-id map
            app_id: entry.app_id.clone(),
            title: entry.title.clone(),
            tag: None, // union: protocols::toplevel_tag where surfaced
            placement: WindowPlacement {
                workspace: entry.workspace,
                x: geo.loc.x,
                y: geo.loc.y,
                width: geo.size.w.max(1),
                height: geo.size.h.max(1),
                maximized: layout == WindowLayout::Maximized,
                fullscreen: layout == WindowLayout::Fullscreen,
                minimized: runtime.manager().is_minimized(entry.id),
                sticky: runtime.manager().is_sticky(entry.id),
            },
        });
        let _ = floating; // geometry saved is current; layout flags say how
    });
    if let Err(e) = logout_save(rows, active, prefs) {
        eprintln!("tuna-compositor: restore: shutdown save failed: {e}");
    }
}
```

Caveat: `WindowManager::geometry` returns the CURRENT (possibly maximized)
geometry; the layout flags record how to reinterpret it, and
apply_restored_placement re-applies size before flags, so the roundtrip is
consistent. The app-id -> desktop-id map does not exist yet; until it does,
collect() falls back to the app id as the desktop id (covered behavior).

### C. windows.rs -- map-time placement (field + hook in place_committed)

Location: crates/compositor/src/windows.rs.
C1: add a field to WindowManager plus a setter (next to model()/model_mut(),
~line 469):

```rust
// P-SY-08 (#338): placements queued by login_restore_plan.
pending_restore: crate::session_restore::PendingPlacements,

/// Queue restore placements for windows as they map (login path).
pub fn set_pending_restore(
    &mut self,
    placements: crate::session_restore::PendingPlacements,
) {
    self.pending_restore = placements;
}
```

(Initialize `pending_restore: Default::default()` in WindowManager::new.)
C2: in `place_committed`'s per-window loop (~line 1328, inside
`for (id, size) in ready`), after the window's own placement resolves:

```rust
// P-SY-08 (#338): a relaunched window takes its saved placement.
let (app_id, tag) = match self.model.window(id) {
    Some(entry) => (
        entry.app_id.clone(),
        self.windows
            .get(&id)
            .and_then(|w| w.surface.wl_surface())
            .map(|s| crate::protocols::toplevel_tag(&s).tag)
            .flatten(),
    ),
    None => (None, None),
};
if let Some(placement) =
    self.pending_restore.take_for(app_id.as_deref(), tag.as_deref())
{
    crate::session_restore::apply_restored_placement(self, state, id, &placement);
}
```

Caveat: `w.surface.wl_surface()` is illustrative -- use whatever accessor
the map path actually has for the underlying WlSurface at union; app-id-only
matching already covers untagged windows. `sticky` cannot be restored yet:
WindowManager exposes only is_sticky(); restoring it needs a setter
(union followup, e.g. `pub fn set_sticky(&mut self, state: &mut State,
id: u64, sticky: bool) -> bool` flipping ManagedWindow.sticky plus the
model's on_all_workspaces, mirroring move_to_workspace).

### D. Shell preference push (excluded shell files -- shape only)

The shell owns the opt-in UI (Settings-style toggle). It must:
  1. persist the bool (its own settings backend, like idle-delay);
  2. push it into the compositor's live flag on change AND at startup:
     `restore_supported.store(enabled, Ordering::SeqCst);`
     (the Arc<AtomicBool> from startup_session_manager, plumbed through
     the existing shell<->compositor channel -- control.rs is excluded,
     so the plumbing itself is union work);
  3. call the equivalent of clear_at(session_file_path()) when the user
     turns restore OFF (compositor already exposes clear_at; shell just
     needs to invoke the path, or the compositor can clear on the
     true->false transition -- union choice).

## Union notes

- Single-file change: session_restore.rs + this log (+ already-pushed
  example fix f9a57b3c). No other file modified on this lane.
- instance_id kept OUT of the JSON snapshot on purpose (secrets policy:
  no tokens); instance continuity is registry-lifetime by design.
- Terminal=true apps are refused by the launcher with ErrorKind::Unsupported
  (needs a terminal emulator integration -- union followup if wanted).
- Crash leftovers: a power cut between temp write and rename can leave a
  hidden `.session.*.tmp` file; harmless (hidden, tiny, unique names never
  collide) -- no janitor added, flag if union wants one.
- EnvGuard serializes XDG-mutating tests; the pre-existing
  snapshot_file_defaults_under_state_home was converted to it.
